# About this blog

I am passionately interested in teaching mathematics and probability theory intuitively without compromising on the technicalities.
I also take great interest in programming and believe it is a creative and aesthetic outlet for deconstructing complex ideas, particularly when expressed with typed languages.
I also take great joy in applying these subjects to personal electronics projects.
My intent for this blog is for it to be a place to share these interests and teach my favorite concepts.
Hopefully, this will be done in a unique way: for it to be more technical than popular-science YouTube channels, more interactive and example-driven than textbooks, and less stuffy than research papers [[1](#paper-joke1), [2](#paper-joke2), [3](#paper-joke3), [4](#paper-joke4), [5](#paper-joke5)].

