# Who am I?

I live in Santa Barbara where I work for [Toyon Research Corporation](https://www.toyon.com/) as a Senior Analyst, solving navigation problems for the Antennas and RF-systems team.
Prior to this, I was a Ph.D. student in mathematics at UCSB.
Rats are my favorite animals, but nowadays my animal-time is spent with my girlfriend's crazy dog.
I enjoy cooking, playing the drums, hiking, bicycling (casually, not a speed-racer), snowboarding, and--dare I say it--long walks on the beach (except for the sand between my toes).
I have always had a habit of mindlessly spending hours focused on math and programming problems, so I take great solace in meditation and the cognitive framing it offers for best enjoying life.

## Connect with me!

I am not on social media, I am bad at texting, and I have a very dense work schedule.
However, I would love to connect and collaborate on projects with anyone who is interested in the same topics as me.
I would also appreciate any sort of feedback for this blog or hear of other related resources.
Feel free to email me at `matthew@URL-OF-THIS-WEBSITE` to reach out.

> I often see people offering their email in a cryptic fashion, e.g. above or `matthew at rodent dot club`.
> Is that because there are actually that many bots looking to email me junk?
> I actually rarely get junk mail, but I may as well play it safe like the cool kids.
> My phone on the other hand?
> Awful. I get like 100 junk calls and texts per day, no matter how many numbers I block.

# Let's goooo! 🏂

The site is split into _posts_ and _sequences_.
Posts are bite-sized musings that one would typically see in a blog.
Sequences are more long-form writings that are comparable to a book.
While I will try to keep pages consistent for posterity, I expect that some posts will be combined over time into sequences.
